---
import Layout from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import {
	SITE_TITLE,
	SITE_DESCRIPTION,
	SITE_EMAIL,
	SITE_GITHUB,
	SITE_LINKEDIN,
	SITE_X,
} from "../consts";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import deannePhoto from "../assets/images/deanne.png";
import cv from "../assets/docs/DeanneSmeaton_UpdatedCV2023_public.pdf";
---

<Layout
	title={`${SITE_TITLE}: About Me`}
	description="A little more about Deanne Smeaton, her journey as a developer, the work she has done, and what she enjoys building."
>
	<article>
		<section>
		<h1>About Me</h1>
		<Image
			src={deannePhoto}
			alt="Photo of Deanne Smeaton"
			class="about-photo"
		/>
		<blockquote>
			{SITE_DESCRIPTION}
		</blockquote>
	</section>
		<section>
			<p>
				Hello, I’m Deanne. I’m a software engineer based in New Zealand,
				with over a decade of experience building software and solving
				problems across the full stack.
			</p>
			<p>
				I enjoy taking complicated problems and turning them into
				practical, maintainable solutions. My work has taken me from web
				applications and APIs through to cloud infrastructure,
				deployment automation, edge devices and distributed systems.
			</p>
			<p>
				These days, I work as a Technical Lead, where I get to move
				between writing code, designing systems, solving technical
				problems and helping projects move forward. I still love getting
				into the details and figuring out how things work.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>What I work with</h2>
			<p>
				My background is primarily in the .NET ecosystem, but I’ve
				worked across a range of technologies including TypeScript,
				React, Node.js, PostgreSQL, AWS and Azure. I’m less interested
				in being tied to a particular technology and more interested in
				choosing the right tools for the problem at hand.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>My journey</h2>
			<p>
				I started my career through the Auckland Council Graduate
				Programme before joining their Web & Mobile team, where I
				progressed to Senior Software Developer. I worked across a range
				of web projects, including customising content management
				systems and applications used by Auckland Council.
			</p>
			<p>
				I later joined Developers Institute, where I mentored aspiring
				developers and helped teach full-stack development, application
				security and software development practices. That experience
				gave me a real appreciation for sharing knowledge and helping
				other developers grow.
			</p>
			<p>
				I then joined Stanbury Electrical Engineering, where my role has
				grown from software development into technical leadership. I
				work across the full stack as well as cloud infrastructure,
				deployment, edge computing and system architecture, helping
				design and build software that connects real-world electrical
				systems with modern software platforms.
			</p>
			<p>
				Today, I’m a Technical Lead, balancing hands-on development with
				technical direction, problem solving and helping projects move
				forward.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>A little more</h2>
			<p>
				This site is my little corner of the web. It’s where I keep
				track of things I’m building, things I’m learning, and
				occasionally things I’ve found interesting enough to write
				about.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you’d like to see more of my professional experience, you can
				view my <a href={cv} target="_blank">cv</a>, find me on <a href={SITE_LINKEDIN} target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>, 
				or <a href={SITE_X} target="_blank">X</a> or have a look through my
				<a href={SITE_GITHUB} target="_blank"> GitHub projects</a>.
			</p>
			<p>You can also send me an <a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>email</a>⁠￼.</p>
		</section>
	</article>
</Layout>


